TOP — LIVE CPU AND TASK VIEWER

Usage: top [seconds]    (default 1, range 1..60)
Keys: q quit (restores terminal).
Sources: /proc/cpu (newest completed sample), /proc/tasks,
         /proc/uptime, /proc/context_switches.
CPU usage is a system-wide approximation; per-task CPU % unavailable.
Uses one of six task slots. Needs an ANSI terminal >= 80 columns.
MCP: use persistent PTY terminal_send/terminal_read, not execute_command.
